<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue id="7afb-39e6-f81d-588b" name="Early Ptolemaic" revision="3" battleScribeVersion="2.03" authorName="Jono Firth" authorUrl="https://www.greatescapegames.co.uk/uploads/images/wysiwyg/home-shortcuts/coe/earlyclassical/Early_Ptolemaic_Feb_28th_2012.pdf" library="false" gameSystemId="c749-87c2-0d4a-5e29" gameSystemRevision="12" xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema">
  <readme>This army list covers Ptolemaic Successor forces in Egypt from the death of Alexander the Great to the death of Ptolemy IV Philopater. During this period the Ptolemaic (or Lagid) Dynasty established itself in Egypt, adopting many of the Pharonic religious doctrines. This list includes the ‘high water mark’ Battle of Raphia in 217 BCE. After this period, the Ptolemaic Kingdom was often torn apart with internal divisions, leading to Civil Wars, and came under the increasing domination of Rome, which finally took complete control after the death of Cleopatra VII (with Marcus Antonius) in 30 BCE. It was, therefore, the longest-lived of all the Successor Kingdoms. Enemies include the other Successor States, especially Seleucid and Antigonid.

An Early Ptolemaic army must include a General, at least one unit of Klerouchoi Cavalry and at least one unit of Klerouchoi Phalangites.</readme>
